<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh procures 12 locomotives from Germany.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh procures 12 locomotives from Germany.</headline>
<dateline>CHITTAGONG, Bangladesh 1997-03-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangladesh has procured 12 locomotives worth $27.30 million from Germany for improving train services in the country's eastern zone, railway officials said on Sunday.</p>
<p>They said nine locomotives had already arrived in Chittagong, headquarters of the eastern railway. Three others are expected to be delivered soon.</p>
<p>The locomotives were built by Germany's biggest manufacturer in the field, Adtranz Germany, the officials said.</p>
<p>Bangladesh bought nine locomotives from Germany in 1995, they said without giving details.</p>
</text>
